    <string name="pillow_speaker.auto_play">Play when it connects</string>
    <string name="pillow_speaker.auto_play_summary">Starts the current book whenever the speaker connects</string>
    <string name="pillow_speaker.force_stop_note">If bVoice has been force-stopped (App info → Force stop), Android will not wake it when the speaker connects, and nothing plays. An automation that opens bVoice when the speaker connects covers that case — for example a Bixby Routine on Samsung (If: Bluetooth device connected → Then: open bVoice), MacroDroid, or Tasker. If you have set one up, this is the reminder that it is there.</string>
    <string name="pillow_speaker.disconnect">Disconnect after a pause</string>
    <string name="pillow_speaker.disconnect_note">Only the media connection is dropped. If the speaker also connects for calls, it stays "connected for calls" and will not switch itself off: turn off Phone calls for it in Android\'s Bluetooth settings (the cog next to the device).</string>
    <plurals name="pillow_speaker.disconnect_summary">
        <item quantity="one">After %d minute paused, so the speaker can switch itself off</item>
        <item quantity="other">After %d minutes paused, so the speaker can switch itself off</item>
    </plurals>
    <string name="pillow_speaker.test_summary">Test: disconnect the speaker now, then watch whether it reconnects by itself.</string>
